Theorem DP-1: needs_ownership_events truth table — Owned AND non-Dead AND not is_scalar

  Preconditions:
    - `is_rc_needed` is the historical implementation name for whether a
      logical ownership event is required; it does not select a physical
      reference-counting mechanism
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - needs_ownership_events : AimsState -> Bool per Annex E §AIMS DP-1 +
      Appendix C truth table
    - is_scalar(s) per §1.8 L-9 — SCALAR is sentinel, NOT a lattice element
    - DP-1 is a pure boolean predicate over Access x Consumption x is_scalar;
      Cardinality / Uniqueness / Locality / Shape / Effect are non-load-bearing
      for the DP-1 obligation

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState (canonical).
      needs_ownership_events(s)
        <=> (s.access = O AND s.consumption != Dead AND NOT is_scalar(s))

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Exhaustive enumeration over the canonical (Access x Consumption x
          is_scalar) product per Appendix C truth table:
            2 Access x 4 Consumption x 2 is_scalar = 16 input states.
      (b) Soundness equality — for every enumerated row, the predicate value
          equals the Appendix C row partition value.

    Part (a) — Appendix C row partition (4 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: Access = Borrowed, any Consumption, any is_scalar -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (first conjunct s.access = O fails).
      Row 2: Access = O, Consumption = Dead, any is_scalar -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (second conjunct s.consumption != Dead
          fails).
      Row 3: Access = O, Consumption != Dead, is_scalar = true -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (third conjunct NOT is_scalar fails).
      Row 4: Access = O, Consumption != Dead, is_scalar = false -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (all three conjuncts hold); s carries a
          managed owned non-scalar value carrying a logical ownership obligation.

    Part (b) — coverage gate:
      The 4 rows partition the 16 product states:
        Row 1: 1 x 4 x 2 = 8 states.
        Row 2: 1 x 1 x 2 = 2 states.
        Row 3: 1 x 3 x 1 = 3 states.
        Row 4: 1 x 3 x 1 = 3 states.
      Total: 8 + 2 + 3 + 3 = 16. Exhaustive coverage; no uncovered rows.

    Negative-direction witness:
      DP-1 = true on EXACTLY the 3 Owned x non-Dead x non-scalar states
      (Linear / Affine / Unrestricted x is_scalar=false). Every other
      enumerated row yields false. Confirms the conjunction is tight.

    Live-variable set typed pre-pass dependency: NOT REQUIRED for DP-1
    (DP-1 is a pure boolean predicate over canonical AimsState dimensions;
    only DP-5 + DP-9 consume live-variable / borrow_sources /
    project_alias_sources / IC-3 contract typed pre-passes per
    Annex E §AIMS DP-5 / DP-9 + the proof-checker design
    Engine-per-Category-Inventory DP row).

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix C row enumeration across 16 states
        per section_05::verify_dp1_needs_ownership_events; the verifier checks the
        soundness equality predicate-vs-row-partition on every enumerated
        row and emits Fail on any divergence)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-1 via 16-state enumeration over (Access x Consumption x is_scalar) per Annex E §AIMS DP-1 + Appendix C
